data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":1224,"item_id":"fc_063754afc2950769016adb33626bd08191862dde6edd59d962","output_index":3,"arguments":"{\"artifact_json\":\"{\\\"inference\\\":\\\"R001\\\",\\\"packet_sha256\\\":\\\"7b074f11e55ebc02dca16b49ff49ca5debf8be1f8d24ed043eff8f4272da76b3\\\",\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"FAIL\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"Packet-only mathematical review of the supplied text and the declared Yui rules. Input boundary: packet.json plus SKILL.md, references/audit-a.md, references/self-containment.md, and the relevant NL0 format rules. No source proof, other inference body, original task, or external theorem was used. This does not authenticate carrier identity, canonical hash binding, or transmitted-material readback, which are outside this review. First unsupported implication: S002 calls e_0,...,e_lambda a basis, but the packet has not proved that assertion. S001 gives action formulas but does not establish nonvanishing/linear independence and spanning of these vectors from H004. Thus the matrix units, coordinate projections, subsequent lattice decomposition, and the claimed irreducibility are not established by this argument as written. No repair is supplied.\\\",\\\"checks\\\":{\\\"inputs\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"H001-H004 are the direct inputs listed for R001; their stated parameter and module conditions are consistent with the uses in S001-S005. The packet supplies no additional mathematical premise, and none is assumed here.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/inputs\\\",\\\"/inputs/0\\\",\\\"/inputs/1\\\",\\\"/inputs/2\\\",\\\"/inputs/3\\\"]},\\\"argument\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"FAIL\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"The first unsupported implication is S002's transition to a basis e_0,...,e_lambda: there is no local proof that these vectors form a basis. Formulas from iterating the sl2 relations do not, by themselves, establish that basis assertion. The matrix-unit constructions and later coordinate/basis arguments depend on it.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/argument/0\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/1\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/2\\\"]},\\\"dependency_accounting\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"FAIL\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"No external theorem is named or listed, but an essential fact—the e_i are a basis—is used in S002 without being an input or proved local fact. It is not licensed by the calculation-policy text.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/argument/1\\\",\\\"/logic/calculations\\\"]},\\\"output\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"FAIL\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"The intended output is the stated nonzero irreducibility property, but the argument does not establish it because its matrix-unit and coordinate arguments rely on the unproved basis assertion.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/output/statement\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/1\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/4\\\"]},\\\"scope\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"The text introduces W as arbitrary at S005 and uses the nonzero-W argument and positive dimension to address the zero/nonzero alternatives. No unsupported escape of a temporary assumption or witness is the primary defect; scope does not cure the missing basis proof.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/locals/12\\\",\\\"/inference/locals/13\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/4\\\"]},\\\"applicability\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"There are no E/M source applications. H001-H004 are used as direct conditional premises; no separate external-source application mapping is needed. This judgment does not validate consequences not proved from those inputs.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/inputs\\\",\\\"/inference/applications\\\"]},\\\"statement_closure\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"The packet gives the full input and output statements, including the principal module and invariant-subspace condition. The unproved basis property is an argument gap, not omitted content in the stated output.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inputs/3/statement\\\",\\\"/output/statement\\\"]},\\\"object_closure\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"FAIL\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"The main object declarations and local introductions are mostly explicit, but the claimed basis use of e_i in S002 is not supported by an existence/independence/spanning argument. Subsequent matrix units are defined and used as though that basis were established.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/locals/2\\\",\\\"/inference/locals/5\\\",\\\"/inference/locals/6\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/1\\\"]},\\\"dependency_closure\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"FAIL\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"Reverse-reading the prose reveals an unaccounted factual dependency: that e_0,...,e_lambda is a basis. H004 states dimension and highest-weight/irreducibility data, but R001 does not derive the basis fact. Downstream S002-S005 depend on it.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inputs/3/statement\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/0\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/1\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/2\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/3\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/4\\\"]},\\\"packet_replay\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"FAIL\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"Judged sufficiency from this packet alone: R001 is not a closed proof because the e_i basis assertion is not proved. This review used only the frozen packet and the declared Yui instructions; it does not claim runtime carrier attestation or independently verify transport/hash binding. Source fidelity is outside this mathematical judgment.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/argument/1\\\",\\\"/warning\\\",\\\"/packet_sha256\\\"]}},\\\"findings\\\":[{\\\"location\\\":\\\"/inference/argument/1/text\\\",\\\"finding\\\":\\\"First unsupported implication: the assertion 'In the basis e_0,...,e_lambda' is not justified by any preceding proof that these vectors are a basis. This blocks the matrix-unit constructions and downstream conclusions. H004's dimension and irreducibility statement alone is not a written local derivation of this particular basis fact.\\\"}]}\"}"}

