ct\\\":\\\"FAIL\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"The intended output is the stated nonzero irreducibility property, but the argument does not establish it because its matrix-unit and coordinate arguments rely on the unproved basis assertion.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/output/statement\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/1\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/4\\\"]},\\\"scope\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"The text introduces W as arbitrary at S005 and uses the nonzero-W argument and positive dimension to address the zero/nonzero alternatives. No unsupported escape of a temporary assumption or witness is the primary defect; scope does not cure the missing basis proof.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/locals/12\\\",\\\"/inference/locals/13\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/4\\\"]},\\\"applicability\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"There are no E/M source applications. H001-H004 are used as direct conditional premises; no separate external-source application mapping is needed. This judgment does not validate consequences not proved from those inputs.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/inputs\\\",\\\"/inference/applications\\\"]},\\\"statement_closure\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"The packet gives the full input and output statements, including the principal module and invariant-subspace condition. The unproved basis property is an argument gap, not omitted content in the stated output.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inputs/3/statement\\\",\\\"/output/statement\\\"]},\\\"object_closure\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"FAIL\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"The main object declarations and local introductions are mostly explicit, but the claimed basis use of e_i in S002 is not supported by an existence/independence/spanning argument. Subsequent matrix units are defined and used as though that basis were established.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/locals/2\\\",\\\"/inference/locals/5\\\",\\\"/inference/locals/6\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/1\\\"]},\\\